---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Tarn collects, uses, and protects information when you use tarnhome.com."
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="legal-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-dates">Effective Date: May 6, 2026 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Last Updated: August 27, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-content">
    <div class="wrap legal-wrap">
      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        VerifiHouse LLC (&ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;our,&rdquo; or &ldquo;us&rdquo;) operates
        Tarn, a website located at tarnhome.com (the &ldquo;Service&rdquo;). This Privacy
        Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard information when you
        use our Service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please read this Privacy Policy carefully. By using the Service, you agree to the
        collection and use of information in accordance with this policy. If you do not
        agree with the terms of this Privacy Policy, please do not use the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information We Currently Collect</h2>
      <p>Tarn is currently in an early stage of operation. Our data collection practices are minimal:</p>

      <h3>2.1 Information You Provide</h3>
      <p>
        We do not currently require you to create an account to use the Service. When you
        use our permit lookup tool, you enter a property address to generate a report; we
        do not separately log that address search. If you submit feedback on a report
        (see Section 2.4 below), the property address and city associated with that report
        are included with your submission so we can review it.
      </p>

      <h3>2.2 Automatically Collected Information</h3>
      <p>
        Like most websites, we may automatically collect certain technical information when
        you visit the Service, including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address and general geographic location</li>
        <li>Browser type and version</li>
        <li>Pages visited and time spent on those pages</li>
        <li>Referring website or source</li>
        <li>Device type and operating system</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information is collected through standard web server logs and, in the future,
        through analytics tools. This data is used solely to understand how the Service is
        used and to improve its functionality.
      </p>

      <h3>2.3 Cookies</h3>
      <p>
        We do not use third-party tracking cookies or advertising cookies. The Service may
        use a session cookie for interface state (for example, remembering which city you
        selected); this session cookie is not used for tracking or advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not currently serve advertising on the Service and have no active advertising
        partners as of the date of this Privacy Policy. If we introduce advertising in the
        future, we will update this Privacy Policy and, where required by law, obtain your
        consent before doing so.
      </p>

      <h3>2.4 Feedback You Submit</h3>
      <p>
        Every page includes a short feedback form (&ldquo;Have thoughts on Tarn?&rdquo;)
        where you can send us a free-text message and, optionally, an email address if
        you&rsquo;d like a reply. Report pages also let you vote on the accuracy of a
        specific finding or of the report overall, with an optional one-line comment &mdash;
        those votes do not ask for an email address, but do include the property address
        and city of the report you&rsquo;re viewing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Feedback submissions are stored and trigger an internal notification to our team so
        we can review and respond to them. If you leave an email address, it is used only
        to reply to you &mdash; it is not added to a mailing list, used for advertising, or
        shared outside the service providers described in Section 5.1.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Future Data Collection</h2>
      <p>Tarn plans to expand its data collection practices as the Service grows. Future data collection may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email addresses collected at signup &mdash; e.g., for a premium feature waitlist, newsletter, or account (separate from the feedback-form email described in Section 2.4, which we already collect today)</li>
        <li>User preferences and search history &mdash; to personalize the Service experience</li>
        <li>Payment information &mdash; collected through a third-party payment processor (e.g., Stripe) when paid features are introduced</li>
        <li>Behavioral analytics &mdash; to understand how users interact with the Service and improve features</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When we begin collecting additional data, we will update this Privacy Policy and,
        where required by law, obtain your consent before collecting new categories of
        information.
      </p>

      <h2>4. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Operate and maintain the Service</li>
        <li>Respond to your inquiries and requests</li>
        <li>Analyze usage patterns to improve the Service</li>
        <li>Comply with applicable laws and regulations</li>
        <li>Protect against fraudulent, unauthorized, or illegal activity</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. How We Share Your Information</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information. We may share information in the following limited circumstances:</p>

      <h3>5.1 Service Providers</h3>
      <p>
        We may share information with third-party vendors and service providers that
        support the operation of the Service, including hosting providers, analytics
        services, and an email delivery provider we use to route feedback-form
        notifications to our team (currently Resend). These parties are authorized to use
        your information only as necessary to provide services to us.
      </p>

      <h3>5.2 Legal Requirements</h3>
      <p>
        We may disclose information if required to do so by law or in response to valid
        requests by public authorities (e.g., a court or government agency).
      </p>

      <h3>5.3 Business Transfers</h3>
      <p>
        If VerifiHouse is involved in a merger, acquisition, or sale of all or a portion of
        its assets, your information may be transferred as part of that transaction. We
        will provide notice before your information is transferred and becomes subject to a
        different privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data Sources</h2>
      <p>
        The permit records and property information displayed by the Service are sourced
        exclusively from public government databases, including city and county open data
        portals, ArcGIS REST services, and similar municipal data systems. We do not
        purchase, license, or receive data from private data brokers or commercial real
        estate data providers. All data sources are government public domain.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain information only for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes
        outlined in this Privacy Policy, unless a longer retention period is required or
        permitted by law. Permit lookup address searches are not separately logged or
        retained. Feedback submissions &mdash; including any email address, property
        address, or city you provide with them, as described in Section 2.4 &mdash; are
        retained so we can review and respond to them and to improve the Service, until we
        no longer need them for that purpose or you ask us to delete them.
      </p>

      <h2>8. California Privacy Rights (CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
      <p>
        If you are a California resident, you may have the following rights under the
        California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and the California Privacy Rights Act
        (CPRA):
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The right to know what personal information we collect, use, disclose, and sell</li>
        <li>The right to delete personal information we have collected</li>
        <li>The right to correct inaccurate personal information we hold about you</li>
        <li>The right to limit the use and disclosure of sensitive personal information</li>
        <li>The right to opt out of the sale of personal information</li>
        <li>The right to non-discrimination for exercising your CCPA rights</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Tarn does not sell personal information. To submit a request to know, delete,
        correct, or limit the disclosure of your personal information, please contact us
        using the information provided in Section 13 (Contact Us) of this Privacy Policy.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Children&rsquo;s Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is not directed to children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe we have
        inadvertently collected information from a child under 13, please contact us
        immediately.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We implement reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to
        protect information against loss, theft, unauthorized access, disclosure,
        alteration, and destruction. However, no method of internet transmission or
        electronic storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>
        The Service may contain links to third-party websites, including links to primary
        government data sources (EPA, USGS, city and county departments). This Privacy
        Policy does not apply to those third-party websites. We encourage you to review the
        privacy policies of any third-party sites you visit.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any
        material changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the
        effective date. Your continued use of the Service after any changes constitutes
        your acceptance of the revised Privacy Policy.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact us at:</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Company:</strong> VerifiHouse LLC<br />
        <strong>Email:</strong> privacy@tarnhome.com<br />
        <strong>Website:</strong> tarnhome.com<br />
        <strong>Mailing Address:</strong> 202 N Cedar Ave, Ste 1, Owatonna, MN 55060
      </p>

      <h2>14. Governing Law</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy is governed by the laws of the State of Minnesota, without
        regard to its conflict of law provisions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-hero {
    padding: 3rem 0 2rem;
    background: var(--charter-navy);
    color: var(--cream);
  }
  .legal-hero h1 {
    color: var(--cream);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .legal-dates {
    opacity: 0.75;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .legal-content {
    padding: 3rem 0 4rem;
  }
  .legal-wrap {
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .legal-wrap h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
  }
  .legal-wrap h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .legal-wrap h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--charter-navy);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-wrap p,
  .legal-wrap li {
    color: var(--slate);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }
  .legal-wrap ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1em;
  }
  .legal-wrap li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .legal-wrap strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
